From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:53:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ui: add wasmfb, a shared-memory display and input backend for
 the browser

QEMU-Wasm runs QEMU's main loop in a Web Worker while the canvas lives on
the browser main thread.  wasmfb publishes the location of the current
DisplaySurface in the shared linear memory (porty_fb_poll) so JavaScript can
blit it without an extra copy inside QEMU, and drains a lock-free input ring
(porty_input_event) from the main loop into ui/input.c.

Native builds compile the same code; PORTY_FB_DUMP and PORTY_INPUT_SCRIPT
exist so the backend can be tested without a browser.
---
 qapi/ui.json   |   8 +-
 ui/meson.build |   1 +
 ui/wasmfb.c    | 474 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 482 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 ui/wasmfb.c

